Regional Market Insights
•	Asia-Pacific: The undisputed leader in travel retail cosmetics, accounting for over 60% of global sales. China, South Korea and Japan dominate with sophisticated consumers and exceptional airport retail environments like Seoul's Incheon and Singapore's Changi.
•	Europe: Maintains strength through heritage luxury brands and major transit hubs like Paris, London and Frankfurt. The region benefits from intra-European tourism and price advantages over domestic markets.
•	Middle East: Dubai and Doha airports lead with extravagant beauty halls catering to transit passengers and luxury gift shoppers, particularly for prestige fragrances.
•	North America: Focuses on convenience and discovery-driven shopping experiences, with strong performance in premium skincare and mini-size product bundles.
•	Latin America: Shows promising growth potential through upgraded airport retail spaces in Brazil and Mexico targeting U.S.-bound travelers.
